DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250317
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250318
SUMMARY:Mississippi: Pass-through entity return (commonly Form 84-105\; not
  independently confirmed this session) due
DESCRIPTION:Mississippi PTE return due the 15th day of the 3rd month after 
 year-end. Exact form number not independently confirmed this session (widel
 y cited as Form 84-105\, but the fetched source did not state the form numb
 er directly). Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states th
 e general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-spec
 ific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with eve
 ry other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift po
 licy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oregon
  all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal US 
 government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, this 
 entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to March 
 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention\,
  not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specific 
 state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Mississippi PTE r
 eturn due the 15th day of the 3rd month after year-end. Exact form number n
 ot independently confirmed this session (widely cited as Form 84-105\, but 
 the fetched source did not state the form number directly). Automatic exten
 sion upon timely filing MS's Application for Extension with any tax due pai
 d\; a federal extension is accepted in lieu of an MS extension if no tax li
 ability exists. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source states 
 the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-sp
 ecific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with e
 very other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shift 
 policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Oreg
 on all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal U
 S government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, thi
 s entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to Marc
 h 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift convention
 \, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this specifi
 c state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | Authority: Miss
 issippi Department of Revenue FAQ\, direct fetch this session: "PTE returns
  are due on or before the 15th day of the 3rd month following the close of 
 the taxable year" and "Taxpayers requesting an extension of time must remit
  the tax due with the proper Mississippi Application for Extension... to re
 ceive an automatic extension." | Source: https://www.dor.ms.gov/business/bu
 siness-tax-frequently-asked-questions | This date is computed from a recurr
 ence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm against th
 e cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
